msgid ""
"# Topographic Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a visualisation with green colours representing lowland "
"elevations and earth colours as mountainous elevations. The script uses "
"discrete classes rather than the continuous visualisations in the other DEM "
"layers.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"
msgstr ""
"# Visualisation topographique\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ce script renvoie une visualisation avec des couleurs vertes représentant "
"les élévations des basses terres et des couleurs terrestres pour les "
"élévations montagneuses. Le script utilise des classes discrètes plutôt que "
"des visualisations continues dans les autres couches DEM."

msgid ""
"# Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a color visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Visualisation en couleurs\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ce script renvoie une visualisation en couleur du modèle numérique "
"d'élévation, à l'aide d'une fonction colorBlend, attribuant des couleurs "
"naturelles continues du terrain aux limites d'élévation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Plus d'informations "
"[ici.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Grayscale Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a grayscale visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"
msgstr ""
"# Visualisation en niveaux de gris\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ce script renvoie une visualisation en niveaux de gris du modèle numérique "
"d'élévation, à l'aide d'une fonction colorBlend, attribuant des couleurs "
"continues aux bordures d'élévation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Plus d'informations "
"[ici.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"

msgid ""
"# Sepia Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a sepia visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"
msgstr ""
"# Visualisation sépia\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ce script renvoie une visualisation sépia du modèle numérique d'élévation, "
"à l'aide d'une fonction colorBlend, attribuant des couleurs continues aux "
"bordures d'élévation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Plus d'informations "
"[ici.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"

