msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Le Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index est similaire au Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) mais s'utilise dans les zones où le couvert végétal "
"est faible (< 40 %). L'indice est une technique de transformation qui "
"minimise l'influence de la brillance du sol sur les indices de végétation "
"spectraux faisant intervenir les longueurs d'onde du rouge et du proche "
"infrarouge (NIR). L'indice est utile pour analyser les jeunes cultures, les "
"régions arides à végétation clairsemée et les surfaces de sol nu.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Plus d'informations "
"[ici](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) et "
"[ici.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"L'indice de neige par différence normalisée de Sentinel-2 permet de "
"distinguer les nuages de la couverture neigeuse, car la neige absorbe la "
"lumière dans l'infrarouge à ondes courtes mais réfléchit la lumière "
"visible, alors que les nuages sont généralement réfléchissants dans les "
"deux longueurs d'onde. La couverture neigeuse est représentée en bleu vif "
"et lumineux.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Plus d'informations "
"[ici](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

